{
  "version": 2,
  "adopted": "2026-01-01",
  "timezone": "",
  "_comment": "Single source of truth for memory budgets, owners, max ages, tags, schedule and the per-briefing read plan. Edit freely. Set 'adopted' to the day you start using Memory v2 so missed-run checks don't flag earlier days. Add a file here and memory_maint.py starts measuring it. 'timezone' is an IANA name like 'America/New_York' (empty = this machine's local time); it sets the clock for schedules, day counts and timestamps.",
